      "description": "Bench-gray card with file-name pill; base card gets a Signal Blue border.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-panel ds-base\"><div class=\"ds-head\"><span class=\"ds-pill\">values-prod.yaml</span><span class=\"ds-detected\">YAML</span></div><div class=\"ds-editor\"><pre class=\"ds-gutter\">1\n2\n3</pre><pre class=\"ds-code\">server:\n  port: 8080\n  host: api</pre></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#fff;--fg:#1d2330;--muted:#667085;--border:#d9dde5;--panel:#f7f8fa;--accent:#3b6fd8;--added:#e3f6e8;--added-bar:#2e9e50;--removed:#fde7e7;--removed-bar:#d0393e;--changed:#fff4cc;--changed-bar:#a87f00;--type:#ffe6d1;--type-bar:#c55a12;--moved:#e1ecff;--moved-bar:#3b6fd8;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--fg)} .ds-panel{padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel);max-width:360px}.ds-panel.ds-base{border-color:var(--accent)}.ds-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:6px}.ds-pill{padding:2px 10px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;background:var(--bg);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600}.ds-detected{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}.ds-editor{display:flex;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:4px;background:var(--bg);overflow:hidden}.ds-gutter,.ds-code{margin:0;padding:6px 8px;font:13px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace}.ds-gutter{background:var(--panel);color:var(--muted);text-align:right}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Diff List",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": null,
      "description": "The ledger: one kind-tinted row per difference with path, description and apply actions.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-list\"><li class=\"ds-added\"><span>aggiunta</span><span class=\"ds-path\">$.db.pool</span><span>presente solo in B</span><span><button class=\"ds-b\">A → B</button></span></li><li class=\"ds-changed\"><span>valore</span><span class=\"ds-path\">$.server.port</span><span>8080 → 9090</span><span><button class=\"ds-b\">A → B</button></span></li></ul>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#fff;--fg:#1d2330;--muted:#667085;--border:#d9dde5;--panel:#f7f8fa;--accent:#3b6fd8;--added:#e3f6e8;--added-bar:#2e9e50;--removed:#fde7e7;--removed-bar:#d0393e;--changed:#fff4cc;--changed-bar:#a87f00;--type:#ffe6d1;--type-bar:#c55a12;--moved:#e1ecff;--moved-bar:#3b6fd8;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--fg)} .ds-list{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}.ds-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:6em minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.5fr) auto;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:6px 10px;border-left:4px solid;cursor:pointer}.ds-list li+li{border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.ds-path{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-added{background:var(--added);border-left-color:var(--added-bar)}.ds-changed{background:var(--changed);border-left-color:var(--changed-bar)}.ds-b{padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:4px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:inherit;font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer}.ds-b:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}.ds-b:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:1px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Change Ledger",
    "overview": "Every difference is an entry in a ledger. It has a kind, a color that says which kind, a path, a line number, and an action that copies it to the other file. The interface is the ledger's paper: neutral, ruled with hairlines, and quiet enough that the entries are what you read. Color is almost never decoration. A colored surface means \"this is a difference of this kind\", and the six kind colors stay consistent across chips, list rows, editor lines, tree nodes and matrix cells.\n\nThe tone is precise but friendly. Layouts are dense, fonts are the system's own, and the chrome sticks to the conventions engineers already know from editors and diff viewers. Softer touches (gently rounded corners, a pill around each loaded file name, a dashed \"+ Aggiungi file\" affordance) keep a tool built for repeated expert use from feeling hostile. Light and dark themes both ship, following the OS through `prefers-color-scheme`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat, bordered surfaces on two neutral levels (paper and bench gray). No shadows.",
      "One interactive accent, Signal Blue, for selection, focus, the base file and links.",
      "A closed set of six difference-kind color pairs (a tint plus a bar), used everywhere a difference appears.",
      "System UI font for chrome, system monospace for anything that is data.",
      "Small, compact controls (2px × 8px padding on secondary buttons, 28px icon buttons)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ledger Color Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "A kind color appears only where that kind of difference appears. Never use Added Green for \"success\", Changed Ochre for \"warning\" or Removed Red for \"delete\" in unrelated chrome. The six pairs are reserved vocabulary."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint-Plus-Bar Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "A difference is always shown as a pale tint with a 4px saturated left bar. Never a full-saturation fill, and never the tint without the bar."
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "Signal Blue is the only interactive color. Selection, focus, the base file and hover all use it. Don't add a second accent."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Data Is Mono Rule",
        "section": "typography",
        "body": "Anything the user could copy into a file or a path field (keys, values, paths, line content) is set in monospace. Labels about data are set in the sans."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Ledger Rule",
        "section": "elevation",
        "body": "Surfaces never cast shadows. If something needs emphasis, change its border or tint, not its elevation."
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do show every difference as a tint plus a 4px left bar in that kind's ledger pair, in every view (chip, row, line, cell).",
      "Do use Signal Blue as the only signal for selection, focus, hover and the base file.",
      "Do set keys, values, paths and file content in system monospace at 13px.",
      "Do keep surfaces flat: Bench Gray panels holding Paper working surfaces, outlined with 1px Hairline borders.",
      "Do give icon-only buttons an `aria-label` and a tooltip.",
      "Do define every new color as a CSS custom property with a dark-theme value under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use the ledger kind colors for generic success, warning or danger states in chrome.",
      "Don't add drop shadows or elevation. Emphasize with borders, tints and outlines.",
      "Don't introduce a second accent color or a web font. The system font stack is the identity.",
      "Don't set data (paths, keys, values) in the sans or as prose.",
      "Don't use full-saturation fills for differences. Tints carry the area and bars carry the signal."
    ]
  }
}
